{"severity":"error","file":"errors/refinement_violated_19.march","start_line":7,"start_col":16,"end_line":7,"end_col":34,"message":"refinement violation: index must not be negative\nargument `n` of `List.nth` does not satisfy precondition `_ >= 0`\nfor example, when `i` is `-1`\nnote: guard the call (e.g. `if i >= 0 && i < len(items) do List.nth(items, i) else … end`) or pass a value known to satisfy it","code":"refinement_violated","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/refinement_violated_19.march","start_line":7,"start_col":32,"end_line":7,"end_col":33,"message":"this argument must satisfy `i >= 0`"},{"file":"errors/refinement_violated_19.march","start_line":6,"start_col":27,"end_line":6,"end_col":28,"message":"`i` comes from here"},{"file":"errors/refinement_violated_19.march","start_line":7,"start_col":7,"end_line":7,"end_col":12,"message":"the call is reached only when this is true"}],"notes":["`List.nth_opt` is `List.nth` without the requirement: it returns `Option` instead of panicking.\n    match List.nth_opt(items, i) do\n      Some(v) -> …\n      None -> …\n    end"],"category":"REFINEMENT"}
